# Vendored third-party trees are data, not instructions (AGENTS.md, "Third-party material").
# Cursor's docs say .cursorignore blocks access to the listed files for Agent, Tab and @-mention references
# (https://cursor.com/docs/context/ignore-files). They do not say whether it also stops rule, AGENTS.md or skill
# discovery in these trees, so this file is a documented access block and nothing stronger.
# Bun tooling (`lumin study`, `lumin adopt`) reads the trees directly.
assets/vendor/
tools/img-to-object/upstream/
.vendor/
